From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:17:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: give Windows voice-host tests the native runtime DLLs
 under Bazel

codex-voice-host links GStreamer and Opus dynamically. Under Bazel on Windows the tests started it without those
DLLs on the PATH, so it exited with STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND (0xC0000135) and every voice-host test target failed.

Backport of upstream openai/codex fixes that are not in a stable release yet:
- #59082 (ac91c14443): the integration tests start the helper with the runtime's bin directory on the PATH.
- #59231 (8da8b0c7f7): installed_client omits one plugin on Windows, so its startup-only fixture still cannot
  initialize the audio runtime.
- #59369 (021fccb04), only defs.bzl and voice-host/BUILD.bazel: the binary unit test gets the runtime on its PATH.
---
